---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';import {withBase} from '../lib/paths';import {site} from '../data/site';const url=(p:string)=>withBase(p,import.meta.env.BASE_URL);
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Meet Nicolás Rodríguez, a Game Producer & Game Designer working across independent and academic games, programming, systems and VFX."><div class="shell"><header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">About / Nicolás Rodríguez</p><h1>Design the experience.<br/><span class="hero-secondary">Help make it real.</span></h1></header><div class="about-layout"><aside><div class="initials" aria-hidden="true">NR<span>.</span></div><p class="eyebrow">Game Producer & Game Designer</p><p>Game direction · Systems design<br/>Programming · VFX</p></aside><div class="prose"><h2>A practice across disciplines.</h2><p>I work on independent and academic games, connecting production and game design with hands-on development. My contributions range from directing projects to programming gameplay systems, building interfaces, and creating VFX.</p><p>I use Godot, Unity, and Unreal Engine across different projects. Each project here explains my role separately from the contributions of the people I work with.</p><h2>Fuenteki Studio</h2><p>Fuenteki is an indie initiative I started in 2024. It is part of my journey as a producer and designer, with projects including Jigsaw Jab, Snowballing, and The Mechamorphosis.</p><p><a href={site.studio}>Visit Fuenteki Studio ↗</a></p><h2>QA at Whiteboard Games</h2><p>From December 2024 to March 2025, I worked remotely as a QA Tester intern on Tempus Vitae. I documented bugs in Jira, tested builds, reproduced issues, and verified fixes with Unity debugging tools.</p><p><a href={url('/work/tempus-vitae/')}>My work on Tempus Vitae ↗</a></p><h2>Beyond original games</h2><p>Under the alias Zheyron, I create mods for Kenshi, including Martial Village. My broader work also includes collaborative QA and creative coding experiments.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href={url('/work/')}>Explore the work ↗</a><a class="text-link" href={url('/contact/')}>Get in touch →</a></div></div></div></div></BaseLayout>
